libgphoto2_port/vusb: unplug the virtual camera once a given file exists

A real camera whose cable is pulled during an import fails every later
transfer, and Framehive then reports each remaining file as failed (CLI-013.11).
The virtual PTP camera of the `vusb` port driver (configure --enable-vusb)
always answers. With this patch, once the file that VCAMERA_UNPLUG_WHEN names
exists, every later read or write on the port fails with GP_ERROR_IO and keeps
failing, so a test can let the camera go away when the host has written a
known file, for example the copy of the first file of an import. Without
VCAMERA_UNPLUG_WHEN nothing changes.

When VCAMERA_CONNECTED_WHILE is also set (libgphoto2-vusb-connected.patch),
unplugging renames the file it names to <file>.pulled instead, so the camera
is no longer listed, and transfers fail only while that file is missing: a
test plugs the camera in again by creating the file (CLI-014.9). The marker
<file>.pulled keeps it from being unplugged again, as the library is loaded
again for each open and loses its static state.

It changes only the `vusb` driver, which Framehive installs outside the iolib
folder that the library loads by default. It is written to be offered upstream.

Applied by flake.nix to nixpkgs' libgphoto2.

--- a/libgphoto2_port/vusb/vcamera.c
+++ b/libgphoto2_port/vusb/vcamera.c
@@ -420,6 +420,35 @@
 static struct ptp_dirent *first_dirent = NULL;
 static uint32_t	ptp_objectid = 0;
 
+/* Like pulling the cable of a real camera: once the file VCAMERA_UNPLUG_WHEN
+ * names exists, every later transfer fails. With VCAMERA_CONNECTED_WHILE, that
+ * file is renamed to <file>.pulled once, and transfers fail while it is missing.
+ */
+static int
+unplugged (void) {
+	static int	gone = 0;
+	const char	*path = getenv ("VCAMERA_UNPLUG_WHEN");
+	const char	*connected = getenv ("VCAMERA_CONNECTED_WHILE");
+	struct stat	stbuf;
+
+	if (connected) {
+		/* The library is loaded again for each open, so the marker file keeps the state. */
+		char	pulled[strlen (connected) + sizeof (".pulled")];
+
+		snprintf (pulled, sizeof (pulled), "%s.pulled", connected);
+		if (path && !stat (path, &stbuf) && stat (pulled, &stbuf)) {
+			gp_log (GP_LOG_DEBUG,__FUNCTION__, "%s exists, unplugging the virtual camera", path);
+			rename (connected, pulled);
+		}
+		return stat (connected, &stbuf) != 0;
+	}
+	if (!gone && path && !stat (path, &stbuf)) {
+		gp_log (GP_LOG_DEBUG,__FUNCTION__, "%s exists, unplugging the virtual camera", path);
+		gone = 1;
+	}
+	return gone;
+}
+
